    runs) cat <<EOF
vmforai runs NAME [ID] [-f | --stop] [--clean] [--json]

Lists the tasks given with "vmforai run": ID, agent, state (running, done,
failed, stopped, interrupted), when, and the task. With an ID it shows that
task's output; -f follows it until it ends. --stop ends a task, --clean
deletes the ones that ended. The VM has to be running.

Examples:
  vmforai runs dev
  vmforai runs dev 3 -f
  vmforai runs dev 3 --stop
EOF
